From fe53ac5630fa853eac107aae9e38ef77c2b68beb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herrie <claude.ai@herrie.org>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 19:08:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Handle hardware keyboard input

While an editor is focused the compositor routes every key to whoever holds
the input methods keyboard grab, which is MaliitServer. This plugin never
implemented processKeyEvent(), so hardware keys fell through to
MAbstractInputMethod::processKeyEvent(), which bounces them back to the
application as a keysym rebuilt from the Qt key code. That conversion cannot
express case (Qt::Key_A == XKB_KEY_A), so every letter reached the
application as an unshifted uppercase keysym and got dropped, along with
several shifted symbols.

Handle the keys here instead: text producing keys go through the same editor
path as the on-screen keyboard, so preedit, word prediction and auto-caps
behave identically whichever keyboard is used. Arrows, Tab, Escape, function
keys and modifier shortcuts are still handed back to the application.

This keeps Maliit in Maliit::OnScreen mode, so the on-screen keyboard stays
available alongside the hardware one.
Upstream-Status: Pending
